course: dictionary
lesson: 7892
title: Ransom and the power of a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ransom is money that criminals ask for before they will set a person free, or give back something they have taken. «Francisco Pizarro captured the Inca emperor Atahualpa in 1532 and had him killed in 1533, even after a huge ransom of gold and silver was paid.» The clue words are captured, which means taken by force, and even after, which warns you that paying did not save him.
explain: As a verb, to ransom someone means to pay to free them. Long ago, kings and knights were often captured in battle and then ransomed. King Richard the Lionheart was held and ransomed between 1192 and 1194. Try your meaning in the sentence: «They paid to free the king» makes sense, so ransom fits.
explain: Some phrases use ransom in a different way. «The gang held the whole town to ransom» means they forced people to obey by threatening them. «That painting cost a king's ransom» means it was very, very expensive. Read the words around the phrase, because they tell you which meaning you need.
fact: A ransom is money demanded by criminals to free a person they have kidnapped, or to give back something they have taken.
fact: To ransom someone is to pay to free them, or to hold them until money is paid.
fact: «Hold to ransom» means forcing people to do something by threatening them.
fact: «A king's ransom» means a huge amount of money.
fact: «Ransomware» is a computer virus that locks your files until money is paid.
exercise: «Francisco Pizarro captured the Inca emperor Atahualpa in 1532 and had him killed in 1533, even after a huge ransom of gold and silver was paid.» What is the ransom in this sentence? | *Gold and silver paid to free a captured ruler | A new castle built by the Inca | A gift of food for the army | A map of the sea
exercise: «The gang held the whole town to ransom.» What does hold to ransom mean? | Rebuild the town hall | Give the town a big party | *Force people to obey by threatening them | Build a wall around the town
exercise: Find and copy one word that means to pay to free someone. | forest | *ransom | river | castle
test: «The computer virus locked every file until the owners paid money.» What is this kind of virus called? | Bookmark | Screensaver | *Ransomware | Wallpaper
test: «That diamond cost a king's ransom.» What does «a king's ransom» mean here? | *A huge amount of money | A safe place to hide | A small coin | A gift from a king
exam: In «Francisco Pizarro captured the Inca emperor Atahualpa in 1532 and had him killed in 1533, even after a huge ransom of gold and silver was paid», what does even after tell you? | *Paying the ransom did not stop the killing | It shows the ransom saved his life | It shows the gold was lost in a storm | It shows the ransom was small
